                                                                  9625 1451  168
  Models and parameters used in the CCONE/4/ calculation          9625 1451  169
  1) Coupled channel optical model                                9625 1451  170
     Levels in the rotational band were included. Optical model   9625 1451  171
     potential and coupled levels are shown in Table 1.           9625 1451  172
                                                                  9625 1451  173
  2) Two-component exciton model/9/                               9625 1451  174
    * Global parametrization of Koning-Duijvestijn/10/            9625 1451  175
      was used.                                                   9625 1451  176
    * Gamma emission channel/11/ was added to simulate direct     9625 1451  177
      and semi-direct capture reaction.                           9625 1451  178
                                                                  9625 1451  179
  3) Hauser-Feshbach statistical model                            9625 1451  180
    * Moldauer width fluctuation correction/12/ was included.     9625 1451  181
    * Neutron, gamma and fission decay channel were included.     9625 1451  182
    * Transmission coefficients of neutrons were taken from       9625 1451  183
      coupled channel calculation in Table 1.                     9625 1451  184
    * The level scheme of the target is shown in Table 2.         9625 1451  185
    * Level density formula of constant temperature and Fermi-gas 9625 1451  186
      model were used with shell energy correction and collective 9625 1451  187
      enhancement factor. Parameters are shown in Table 3.        9625 1451  188
    * Fission channel:                                            9625 1451  189
      Double humped fission barriers were assumed.                9625 1451  190
      Fission barrier penetrabilities were calculated with        9625 1451  191
      Hill-Wheler formula/13/. Fission barrier parameters were    9625 1451  192
      shown in Table 4. Transition state model was used and       9625 1451  193
      continuum levels are assumed above the saddles. The level   9625 1451  194
      density parameters for inner and outer saddles are shown in 9625 1451  195
      Tables 5 and 6, respectively.                               9625 1451  196
    * Gamma-ray strength function of Kopecky et al/14/,/15/       9625 1451  197
      was used. The prameters are shown in Table 7.               9625 1451  198
